113615.description:
When creating an Ingest Pipeline, it's currently possible to create a processor, which is not a map:
PUT _ingest/pipeline/test
{
  "processors": [
    {
      "script": """ctx.test=2;"""
    }
  ]
}
This is accepted by Elasticsearch, however, the expected syntax should be:

PUT _ingest/pipeline/test
{
  "processors": [
    {
      "script": {
        "source": "ctx.test=2;"
      }
    }
  ]
}
This causes API GET _ml/trained_models/_stats (which iterates over all processors and verify that they are maps) to fail with the error:

[2024-09-26T09:55:24,326][WARN ][o.e.x.m.MachineLearningUsageTransportAction] [node-1] Failed to get inference usage to include in ML usage
java.lang.ClassCastException: class java.lang.String cannot be cast to class java.util.Map (java.lang.String and java.util.Map are in module java.base of loader 'bootstrap')
I would expected Elasticsearch to refuse processors that are not Maps.
